From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/wayland: pvr: clients default to swrast (MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW=1 opts in)

On the SGX540, compositors (mutter, via GBM) render fine with the pvr
driver, but EGL Wayland clients' GPU buffers crash gnome-shell inside the
closed SGX blob. Make Wayland clients use swrast + wl_shm by default. The GBM
platform (the compositor) is unaffected.
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-20 00:20:59.633863558 +0000
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-20 00:20:59.733862238 +0000
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include "loader.h"
 #include "util/u_vector.h"
 #include "util/anon_file.h"
+#include "util/debug.h"
 #include "eglglobals.h"
 
 #include <wayland-egl-backend.h>
@@ -2151,7 +2152,12 @@
 EGLBoolean
 dri2_initialize_wayland(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 {
-   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware)
+   /* pvr: Wayland clients render with swrast and present through wl_shm,
+    * unless MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW=1. Client GPU buffers crash compositors inside
+    * the SGX blob (gnome-shell, libGLESv2_PVR_MESA). Compositors use the GBM
+    * platform and keep the GPU. pmos-galaxy docs/bringup.md B15. */
+   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware ||
+       !env_var_as_boolean("MESA_PVR_WAYLAND_HW", false))
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(disp);
    else
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_drm(disp);
